<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xliff xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:2.0" xmlns:swi18n="https://step-wise.com/ns/i18n" version="2.1" srcLang="en">
	<file id="catalog">
		<group id="meta">
			<unit id="learningGoals">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">The goal of this skill is to show how different skills are combined into a <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">composite skill</pc>. In this skill, students calculate an expression like <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, where they first have to <pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">multiply</pc> numbers and then <pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">add</pc> them.</pc></source>
				</segment>
			</unit>
		</group>
		<group id="theory">
			<unit id="intro">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">After having learned how to <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">multiply numbers</pc> and how to <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">add numbers</pc>, we now combine these skills. Our goal is to calculate <pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">composite expressions</pc>, like for instance <ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></source>
				</segment>
			</unit>
			<unit id="calculationSteps">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:head" swi18n:slot="children">The steps</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">To calculate an expression like <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, you take the following <pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">steps</pc>.</pc><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:list" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Determine the <pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">order</pc> in which operations should be applied. Multiplications is always done before summation, so <ph id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> should be calculated before anything is added up.</pc><pc id="c9" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate the <pc id="c10" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">multiplication(s)</pc>. We turn <ph id="c11" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> into <ph id="c12" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc><pc id="c13" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate the <pc id="c14" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">addition</pc>. This then turns <ph id="c15" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> into <ph id="c16" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> which is the final result.</pc></pc></source>
				</segment>
			</unit>
			<unit id="stepWiseExercises">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:head" swi18n:slot="children">Step-Wise exercises</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">In Step-Wise, when practicing composite skills, it is always possible to <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">split exercises into steps</pc>. These steps are then connected to earlier skills, which you have shown mastery of before. This always allows you to complete the more complicated exercises too: they're just combinations of things you already know!</pc><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Behind the scenes, our skill tracking algorithm will <pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">take every action into account</pc>. If you fail at a specific step (for instance at addition) then your rating for that step will decrease. If it drops too much, you will be suggested to practice this skill separately a bit more. In this way the Step-Wise app coaches you to always practice the skill most relevant to you.</pc></source>
				</segment>
			</unit>
		</group>
		<group id="practice">
			<group id="summationAndMultiplication1">
				<unit id="mainProblem">
					<segment>
						<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:integer-input"><pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="label">Answer</pc><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="prelabel"><ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/></pc></pc></pc></pc></source>
					</segment>
				</unit>
				<group id="step1">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Determine which operation must be applied first.</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:multiple-choice" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:choice" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:a" swi18n:slot="children">Addition comes first, before multiplication.</pc></pc><pc id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:choice" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:b" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplication comes first, before addition.</pc></pc></pc></pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Multiplication always comes before addition.</pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
				<group id="step2">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate the multiplication.</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:integer-input"><pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="label">Step answer</pc><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="prelabel"><ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/></pc></pc></pc></pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">The result of the multiplication is <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
				<group id="step3">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate the addition.</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:integer-input"><pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="label">Final answer</pc><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="prelabel"><ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/></pc></pc></pc></pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">After the multiplication we add everything together. This gets us the final result <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></source>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
				<group id="feedback">
					<group id="order">
						<unit id="incorrect">
							<segment>
								<source>That's not correct. Addition always comes last. (Unless it's prioritized by brackets, which is not the case here.)</source>
							</segment>
						</unit>
						<unit id="correct">
							<segment>
								<source>Yes! Multiplication indeed comes first.</source>
							</segment>
						</unit>
					</group>
				</group>
			</group>
